     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hey all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve got some data with blank lines that should interpreted literally instead of converting to &lt;NA&gt;, so I set na.strings to null:</div><div><br></div><div>r &lt;- read.csv(filename, stringsAsFactors=FALSE, encoding=&quot;UTF8&quot;, na.strings=NULL)<br></div><div><br></div><div>This appears to work fine, but it&#39;s making a simple sapply function behave strangely:</div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt;read.csv(filename, stringsAsFactors=FALSE, encoding=&quot;UTF8&quot;, na.strings=NULL)</div><div>&gt; </div><div>&gt; #check for missing conversions</div><div>&gt; u &lt;- unique(v)</div><div>&gt; i &lt;- which(! u %in% r$varname)</div><div><div>&gt; u[i]</div><div>[1] NA</div></div><div><div>&gt; length(u[i])</div><div>[1] 1</div></div><div><br></div><div>&gt; val &lt;- sapply(u[i], function(x) isTRUE(x == &quot;NA&quot;) | <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466261833000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ajOBiAGL0w4kxhxCxqTum\">is.na</a>(x))</div><div>&gt; val</div><div>&lt;NA&gt; </div><div>TRUE </div></div><div><div><br></div><div></div></div><div><br></div><div>If I check the sapply conditions manually, it returns TRUE without the weird &lt;NA&gt;.</div><div><div>&gt; test &lt;- u[i]<br></div></div><div><div>&gt; isTRUE(test == &quot;NA&quot;) | <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466261833000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ajOBiAGL0w4kxhxCxqTum\">is.na</a>(test)</div><div>[1] TRUE</div></div><div><br></div><div>This problem goes away if I remove na.strings=NULL from read.csv, but then it breaks a different part of the code where I need a blank to not be converted to NA. In short, something weird is going on that I can&#39;t figure out.</div><div><br></div><div>Example code/data attached.</div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks,<br>Erica<br><br>--<br>Erica Rettig<br>Ph.D. Candidate<br>Graduate Group in Ecology, UC Davis</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
