   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi Erica, <div><br></div><div>This is working correctly.  sapply() is returning a named vector, and &lt;NA&gt; is the name of the single element.  Notice that the sapply() in the working block returns a named list, and compare what happens with `sapply(c(zoo = NA_character_), <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466261835000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1YpqWTZE0ZJd9P5kTDbRzk\">is.na</a>)`.  </div><div><br></div><div>I don’t understand why sapply() is returning a named vector in this particular case.  But named vectors will behave like unnamed vectors, except that you have some additional ways of accessing their values.  So you should be able to safely assign this to val and proceed with the rest of your script.  </div><div><br></div><div>If for some reason you really want to get rid of the names, use `names(val) &lt;- NULL` after the sapply().  </div><div><br></div><div>Cheers, </div><div>Dan</div><div><div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">----<br>Daniel J. Hicks<br>Postdoctoral Researcher<br>Data Science Initiative<br>University of California, Davis<br><br>&quot;Cautious, careful people, always casting about to preserve their reputation and social standing, never can bring about a reform. Those who are really in earnest must be willing to be anything or nothing in the world&#39;s estimation.&quot; -- Susan B. Anthony<br><br>Pronouns: Masculine (he/him/his) or neutral (they/them/their)</div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Oct 31, 2018, at 4:35 PM, Erica Rettig &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">erica....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
